  "summary": "Mount Tambora, on Sumbawa in present-day Indonesia, erupted in April 1815, with a climax around 10 April, and was rated VEI 7. Death tolls are attributed differently: NOAA gives 11,000 from pyroclastic flows and over 100,000 from later food shortages, while Munich Re cites some 71,000 directly. The following year was called the Year Without a Summer.",
